A||||15||recluse||fan will NOT shut off, even with car off||||8||
Z||000000||recluse||12-01-2001||12:15 PM||||Last night when i got home and turned the car off the fan kept running. After playing with it for a while i unhooked the battery and went to bed.  This morning i put the original fan switch back in (i was using a low temp switch). and that didnt help.  I unplugged the fan fuse and that didnt help. I couldnt find anything on the subject in my chiltons book.  Is there a relay that could be stuck open/closed somewhere??  Please help!  thanks||||reg||8
Z||000001||johnt671||12-01-2001||12:23 PM||||The fan relay is in front of the drivers side headlight.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||12-01-2001||12:25 PM||||probably is the relay and it is mounted in the left frt corner of frt compartment.(near headlamp assembly)||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||12-01-2001||12:28 PM||||If you are refering to the radiator fan, there is a relay near the left headlight. It is hot at all times. If that relay sticks,(a common problem), the fan will run till the battery is dead, even with the key off. I think there is more on this in Ogre's cave, and several posts in archives. Single speed relays are pretty cheap, two speed fan relays are high and harder to find. First, find the relay on your car, pull the little cover off and see if the contacts are stuck or dirty, sometimes they just need to be cleaned.||||reg||1
Z||000004||recluse||12-01-2001||12:29 PM||||thanks!  i will go check that out right now.||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||12-01-2001||12:35 PM||||Recluse, if that is what it is, change it, & either clean your old one up for a spare or buy two. Keep one for an emergency spare. It's one thing for it to stick and keep running, but a disaster if it just won't close out in the middle of nowhere and you run the risk of burning up an engine. cheap insurance, a lot easier to just plug in a spare than rewiring directly to the fan, just to get home. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||recluse||12-01-2001||12:36 PM||||That was the problem.  I tapped on the relay with the handle of a screw driver and the fan shut right off.  I will take that one apart and clean it or pull one off my parts car.  Thats what i like about this forum, good fast help!  thanks again||||reg||14
Z||000007||theogre||12-01-2001||03:39 PM||||The single speed relays can be taken apart. I had mine fall apart in my hand. It's actually easier to split the case than get the plug off.<P>You should probably replace it. especially if you use the fan allot. Once a relay pits it's contacts it usually keeps doing it until the thing finally is shot.<P>For those of you with 2 speed fans....<P>There is now a schematic in my cave for converting the system to use two standard single speed relays. That is way cheaper than the 2 speed unit and if you fry the low speed one you can just swap connectors until you replace the dead one. (Low speed is used more than high. High only runs when the motor is over heating.)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Marc Harris||12-02-2001||01:08 PM||||This is wierd. <P>I went out this morning and my radiator fan was running as well. I disconnected the battery and logged on to the forum and found this thread. My problem was the relay, too.<P>Coincidence . . . or is it???<P>Marc Harris<BR>San Jose, CA||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||12-02-2001||05:12 PM||||my car did the same exact thing at the Dayton meeting last month. I finally got restarted and drove home. I havent messed with the relay at all and its not done it again yet. I did put a new battery in anyway because it was 4 years old. I build custom headlites over where the relay sits and its a little tougher for me to get too. prob about an hours worth of work. I did put a battery isolator in so if ANYTHING gets left on again, it shuts off power from battery.||||reg||1
Z||000010||recluse||12-02-2001||10:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Marc Harris:<BR><B><P><BR>Coincidence . . . or is it???<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think not!  Do you have a medium metallic 87 GT 5 speed also?||||reg||12
Z||000011||maryjane||12-02-2001||10:46 PM||||Coincidence? I've said it before. One week it will be a bunch of SIMILAR fuel pump problems. Then next week, it seems to be ALL<BR>cooling problems. Then, brake related problems the following week. The're ALIVE I tell you, and can communicate with one another. It's a govt conspiracy of some sort.<BR>Who knows what The Ogre's cooking up in that Cave of his. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Well, the last part was joking, but the rest is accurate..just watch throughout the next few weeks.||||reg||1
